# Mirrors .gitignore, and matters for the same reason: anything copied into an
# image layer ships with that image. A .env or a course export baked into a
# layer is as exposed as a commit — more so if the image is ever pushed.

.git
.gitignore

# Every secret- and data-shaped pattern carries `**/`. Docker matches a bare pattern against the
# context root only, where .gitignore means the same line at any depth, so `.env` alone would keep
# a root .env out of the image and copy one planted under examples/ or src/ straight in (roadmap
# item 39). `**/` matches at the root too.
#
# `data/` is widened with the rest. .gitignore already ignores a directory named `data` at any
# depth, so no tracked path can live under one and widening drops nothing a checkout carries.
**/data/
**/*.imscc
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/secrets/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.token
**/config.local.*
**/instance/
**/private/

**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db

# Any depth, not just the context root: Docker matches a bare pattern against the root only, so
# without `**/` the host's bytecode under src/ and tests/ -- and the absolute path each .pyc was
# compiled under -- rode into the image with COPY (roadmap item 37).
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/*.egg-info/

**/.DS_Store
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.swp

# Not needed at runtime — keeps the image small and the layer set boring.
docs/

# ...but the design tokens ARE needed at runtime. docs/tokens.css is the single source of colour
# and is served verbatim rather than copied into the package, so the image must carry this one
# file out of docs/.
!docs/tokens.css

# ...and the spec is needed by the test suite, which reads the detector inventory out of §05 and
# checks the sample course against it. Only the dev stage copies it; the runtime image does not.
!docs/SPEC.md
